---
import data from '../data/sdk-footprint.json';
const mib = (value: number) => (value / 1048576).toFixed(2);
const c = data.results.find(row => row.id === 'vgi-c')!;
const rust = data.results.find(row => row.id === 'vgi-rust')!;
const metrics = [
  ['artifact_bytes', 'Stripped executable'],
  ['app_bytes', 'Executable + dependencies'],
  ['idle_rss_bytes', 'Warmed RSS'],
  ['peak_rss_bytes', 'Sampled peak RSS'],
] as const;
---

<section id="vgi-sdk-footprint" class="mt-12 scroll-mt-24 border-b border-soil-300 pb-10 dark:border-dark-rule">
  <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sun-700 dark:text-cream-2">VGI application SDKs</p>
  <h2 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-semibold text-soil-900 dark:text-cream">C and Rust: full example workers</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-soil-700 dark:text-cream-2">
    The <code>vgi-c</code> and <code>vgi-rust</code> application workers include catalogs and function execution on top of RPC.
    This separate comparison runs their full integration fixture workers through the same VGI client:
    1,000 scalar <code>double</code> calls, then 200 <code>passthru</code> calls carrying a 1 MiB string.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-soil-700 dark:text-cream-2">
    Measured <time datetime={data.generated_at}>{data.generated_at.slice(0, 10)}</time> · {data.host.chip} · macOS ARM64 ·
    Five fresh processes per implementation · Stdio · One caller and worker · MiB.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-5 text-xs text-soil-700 dark:text-cream-2 sm:hidden">Scroll the table horizontally for dependency sizes and memory.</p>
  <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-soil-300 dark:border-dark-rule" role="region" aria-label="C and Rust VGI SDK worker measurements" tabindex="0">
    <table class="w-full min-w-[720px] text-sm">
      <caption class="sr-only">Full VGI example worker sizes and resident memory in MiB. Memory values are medians of five rounds.</caption>
      <thead class="bg-soil-100 text-soil-900 dark:bg-dark-raised dark:text-cream">
        <tr>
          <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 text-left">Example worker</th>
          {metrics.map(([, label]) => <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 text-right">{label}</th>)}
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="divide-y divide-soil-200 dark:divide-dark-rule">
        {data.results.map(row => (
          <tr class="bg-white dark:bg-dark-panel">
            <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-4 text-left font-normal">
              <span class="font-semibold text-soil-900 dark:text-cream">{row.name}</span>
              <span class="ml-2 qf-figure text-xs text-soil-700 dark:text-cream-2">{row.version}</span>
              <div class="mt-1 flex gap-3 text-xs">
                <a href={`${row.repository}/tree/${row.sha}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="qf-link font-mono">{row.sha.slice(0, 8)}</a>
                <a href={`/benchmarks/sdk/footprint-${row.id}-files.json`} class="qf-link">Files</a>
              </div>
            </th>
            {metrics.map(([key]) => (
              <td data-numeric class="px-4 py-4 text-right text-soil-900 dark:text-cream">
                {mib(row[key])}
                {(key === 'idle_rss_bytes' || key === 'peak_rss_bytes') && (
                  <div class="mt-1 text-xs text-soil-700 dark:text-cream-2">{mib(row[`${key}_min`])}–{mib(row[`${key}_max`])}</div>
                )}
              </td>
            ))}
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-soil-700 dark:text-cream-2">
    Rust uses {((1 - rust.idle_rss_bytes / c.idle_rss_bytes) * 100).toFixed(0)}% less warmed resident memory in this snapshot;
    C’s executable is {((1 - c.artifact_bytes / rust.artifact_bytes) * 100).toFixed(0)}% smaller.
    The C example embeds 17.73 MiB of captured Arrow catalog and function fixtures and decodes catalog data at startup.
    These figures describe the current full fixture workers, including their different catalog storage and dependency sets.
  </p>
  <details class="mt-4 text-sm text-soil-700 dark:text-cream-2">
    <summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-soil-900 dark:text-cream">Measurement details and reproduction</summary>
    <div class="mt-3 max-w-3xl space-y-3 leading-relaxed">
      <p>Both builds use release optimization and stripped symbols. C uses nanoarrow and Rust uses Arrow Rust.
        Non-system dynamic libraries count toward dependencies; system libraries are excluded. Neither needs a separately installed language runtime.
        C uses RPC C at <code>01ab0873</code>; Rust resolves RPC Rust 0.31.3 from the recorded Cargo.lock.</p>
      <p>Every call’s result is checked. Warmed RSS is sampled for 0.5 seconds after the scalar calls;
        peak RSS is sampled at a target 10 ms interval during the 200 pass-through calls. The table gives medians and min–max ranges across five rounds.
        RSS includes shared resident pages and excludes the client. Short-lived peaks may be missed.
        The run uses one fresh worker per round, without worker pooling or shared-memory transport.</p>
      <p>The workload includes VGI binding and stream setup on each invocation. It differs from the RPC conformance workload above;
        its memory figures should be compared within this table.</p>
      <p class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-2">
        <a href="/benchmarks/sdk/footprint.json" class="qf-link">JSON + raw rounds</a>
        <a href="/benchmarks/sdk/footprint.csv" class="qf-link">CSV</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/Query-farm/vgi-rpc-website/blob/main/benchmarks/SDK_FOOTPRINT.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="qf-link">Reproduce the comparison</a>
        <a href={`${c.repository}/blob/${c.sha}/example-worker/fixtures.c`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="qf-link">C fixture loading</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>
</section>
